# --- AI providers ------------------------------------------------------------
# Card/quiz generation is now MULTI-PROVIDER, configured in the app at
# Réglages → Intelligence artificielle (Anthropic, OpenRouter, Ollama,
# OpenAI-compatible). Keys entered there are stored server-side, write-only, and
# never shown again. Generation is unavailable (503) only when NO provider is
# usable.
#
# Optional env fallbacks (retro-compat; the app config takes precedence). NEVER
# commit a real key:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY     — Anthropic (also resolves an `ant auth login` profile)
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY    — OpenRouter
#   OPENAI_API_KEY        — generic OpenAI-compatible endpoints
#   MISTRAL_API_KEY       — Mistral (generation + the dedicated /v1/ocr OCR API)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
#
# Ollama is local, free and needs NO key: if an Ollama server is running
# (default http://localhost:11434), pick it in Réglages and choose an installed
# model — zero cost, fully private.

# --- OpenAI Codex provider (ChatGPT subscription) ----------------------------
# OFF BY DEFAULT. The `openai-codex` provider is inert unless this is EXACTLY
# '1': the device-link routes answer as if the provider did not exist, and it can
# never be resolved for a generation (`resolveCodexConfig`,
# apps/server/src/services/ai-config.service.ts). Turning it on only makes the
# provider selectable — the account is then linked from Réglages → Intelligence
# artificielle, by OAuth device code, and NEVER for the demo account.
# ENGRAM_ENABLE_CODEX=1
#
# HMAC key sealing the short-lived device-link handle (the opaque string the
# browser polls with). Optional: falls back to SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET, then to a
# fixed dev constant when neither is set — acceptable locally, where handles
# never leave the machine. Set a dedicated secret in production if the JWT secret
# is not available. NEVER commit a real value.
# ENGRAM_CODEX_HANDLE_SECRET=
#
# Endpoint overrides — TEST-ONLY. Their single purpose is to point the device
# flow at the local mock server in the verification gate; production always talks
# to the real hosts (https://auth.openai.com, chatgpt.com/backend-api). Setting
# either against a host you do not control would send the OAuth exchange there.
# ENGRAM_CODEX_AUTH_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:4599
# ENGRAM_CODEX_RESPONSES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4599/backend-api/codex/responses

# Postgres connection string — OPTIONAL in local dev. When neither DATABASE_URL
# nor POSTGRES_URL is set, `resolveDatabaseUrl()` (apps/server/src/db/paths.ts)
# falls back to the local Supabase CLI stack:
#   postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# That fallback IS the normal development mode — start the stack with
# `bun run dev:db` (supabase start, Docker daemon running). Set the variable only
# to point at a different database.
#
# `ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:54322` therefore means the local stack is DOWN (Docker
# or `supabase start`), NOT that a variable is missing.
#
# Production is a Supabase CLOUD project (supabase.com). Use the
# session/transaction pooler URL (:6543) for the app; the client already disables
# prepared statements on that port. For DDL, prefer a direct connection:
# migrations read POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING / DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED first.
# On Vercel, the Supabase integration injects POSTGRES_URL — do not set it here.
#
# NEVER commit a cloud credential in this file, and NEVER run a test suite
# against the cloud database.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Postgres used by `bun run test:e2e`. The harness CREATEs and DROPs a throwaway
# database per run, so it only ever accepts a LOCAL host (127.0.0.1, localhost or
# ::1) — any port. A cloud DATABASE_URL is ignored, never inherited. Unset, it
# falls back to the local Supabase stack above, which is what runs it in practice.
# Any other local Postgres works too, e.g. a disposable one:
#   docker run --rm -d -p 54322:5432 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres --name engram-e2e postgres:16
# E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Postgres used by `bun scripts/generate-landing-shots.ts` (landing captures).
# Same rule: a throwaway database on a LOCAL host only, any port. DATABASE_URL is
# deliberately NOT read there (in normal dev it points at the cloud); unset, the
# script uses the local Supabase stack above.
# LANDING_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Port the standalone server listens on (`bun run dev`, and the server the
# Playwright configs boot). Default 3001; the Vite dev server proxies to it.
# Unused on Vercel, where the function is invoked, not listened on.
# PORT=3001

# Timezone. All day/week bucketing (analytics + planning) runs in the process
# timezone; leave unset locally to use the machine's zone. On UTC hosts (e.g.
# Vercel) this MUST be set to the user's zone or the buckets drift by a day.
# See docs/deploy-vercel.md for the full deploy env reference.
# TZ=Europe/Zurich

# --- Test doubles ------------------------------------------------------------
# Swaps the card/quiz generator AND the vision extractor for deterministic fakes
# (apps/server/src/index.ts, which logs a warning on boot). No provider is ever
# called. Set by both Playwright configs so the e2e suite has no network
# dependency and no cost. NEVER set this in production.
# ENGRAM_FAKE_AI=1

# --- Auth (Supabase) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side JWT verification. In prod (Vercel) the Vercel×Supabase integration
# injects SUPABASE_URL automatically — do NOT set it here. Locally, leave it
# empty: the application auth gate is then DISABLED (localhost, no exposure).
# SUPABASE_URL=
# Optional, ONLY to test the login against a LOCAL GoTrue (HS256 path):
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
#
# The anon (publishable) key, read SERVER-SIDE. Public by design — it identifies
# the project and grants nothing on its own. The server needs it for one thing:
# calling GoTrue `token?grant_type=password` for the demo CTA below. Falls back to
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. On Vercel the Supabase integration injects it.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# Test-only auth bypass (like ENGRAM_FAKE_AI). Dev/e2e local only; IGNORED on
# Vercel (VERCEL=1 or NODE_ENV=production). NEVER set this in production.
# ENGRAM_AUTH_DISABLED=1
#

# --- First-run journey (T-049) -----------------------------------------------
# Turns OFF the language/theme → study pace → AI journey that a brand-new account
# is redirected to once (GET /api/onboarding then always answers `disabled`).
# Set by BOTH Playwright configs: their database is created empty for the run, so
# every spec would otherwise open on a "new account" and be redirected out of the
# screen it came to test. Leave it unset in dev and in production — the journey
# never fires for an account that already owns content, nor for the demo.
# ENGRAM_ONBOARDING_DISABLED=1
#
# --- Account CRUD (spec §2, GoTrue Admin API) --------------------------------
# GoTrue service_role key — SERVER ONLY. Enables creating/editing accounts from
# /admin (invite by email or temporary password). Read once by the admin client;
# NEVER exposed in any response or log. On Vercel the Supabase×Vercel integration
# usually injects it — verify before setting. Absent → account creation/edit
# returns a clean 503 (account_mgmt_unavailable); every other feature works.
# NEVER commit a real key.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# Trusted public site base URL for the invitation redirect (amendment A9). MUST be
# server-set (never derived from the request Origin). The invite link lands here,
# then the app routes to /set-password. Prod: https://engram.alexabriel.com
# Local dev fallback if unset: http://localhost:5174
# ENGRAM_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://engram.alexabriel.com

# --- Multi-user (user_id scoping, spec §2bis) --------------------------------
# When the auth gate is NOT enforced (local dev / e2e bypass), the server poses a
# default identity whose `sub` is this value (fallback: 'dev-user'). After the
# 0004 migration backfills existing rows to Alex's Supabase UID, set this to that
# UID locally so the live dashboard (3001/5173) shows the backfilled data —
# otherwise the default 'dev-user' owns nothing and the dashboard looks empty.
# ENGRAM_DEV_USER_ID=20d58a6e-71c6-4af2-b1d4-143c93970f8b
#
# Admin gate (spec §3): only this user may write AI config / use the backup
# routes. On Vercel set it to Alex's UID. Absent in enforced prod → those routes
# fail-closed (403 for everyone). Under the dev bypass the default identity above
# is treated as the admin, so local dev needs nothing here.
# ENGRAM_ADMIN_USER_ID=20d58a6e-71c6-4af2-b1d4-143c93970f8b
#
# Demo account (spec §4, optional). Three independent variables — the reset
# behaviour and the public login are configured separately.
#
# 1) ENGRAM_DEMO_USER_ID — the demo account's Supabase UID. When set, a login as
#    THIS user wipes+reseeds a fresh demo dataset on each new Supabase session,
#    and /api/health reports `demoEnabled:true`. Absent → no reset behaviour.
#    (The same behaviour can be switched on per-account from /admin via the
#    `is_demo` flag, which is why this one is optional even with a demo live.)
#    The demo Supabase user is created BY HAND in the Supabase dashboard, never
#    by the app.
# ENGRAM_DEMO_USER_ID=
#
# 2+3) ENGRAM_DEMO_EMAIL / ENGRAM_DEMO_PASSWORD — the demo account's credentials,
#    used ONLY by `POST /api/demo/session` (the landing's "Essayer la démo" CTA):
#    the server signs in to GoTrue on the visitor's behalf and returns the session
#    tokens. They are SERVER-SIDE ONLY — there is deliberately no `VITE_` twin, the
#    password never reaches the bundle, never appears in a response, an error or a
#    log. NEVER commit the real password.
#
#    The CTA needs all four of SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, ENGRAM_DEMO_EMAIL
#    and ENGRAM_DEMO_PASSWORD. Any one missing → the route answers a clean 503
#    `demo_unavailable`, /api/health reports `demoLoginEnabled:false`, and the
#    landing simply does not render the CTA (it reads that flag at RUNTIME, so
#    turning the demo on needs no front-end redeploy).
#
#    The route is public (the only unauthenticated write route) but reads NOTHING
#    from the caller — no body, no query, no header — so it can never act as a
#    login proxy. It is rate-limited to 10 sessions/minute PER SERVER INSTANCE;
#    on Vercel that is per lambda, so it is not a global guarantee (see the
#    comment at the top of apps/server/src/routes/demo.ts).
# ENGRAM_DEMO_EMAIL=demo@example.com
# ENGRAM_DEMO_PASSWORD=

# --- Web (client, PUBLIC values) ---------------------------------------------
# The anon key is PUBLIC by design (identifies the project, grants nothing). On
# Vercel these are mapped from SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY by vite.config
# (define). Locally, leave empty (web auth OFF). See apps/web/.env.example.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
